2026-10-15 21:21 UTC — added a direct regression for the initial
`tls.config.file` system-property snapshot.

Pinned Java client: 5.5.1, source commit
`efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.

The invoked Java oracle initializes `TlsSystemConfig.tlsConfigFile` from a
first properties file, changes the JVM system property to a second file with
the opposite `tls.test.mode.enable` value, then builds a TLS context. The
fixture records that Java still uses the first file. The Rust integration case
re-enters itself in a fresh test process so the process-wide property `OnceLock`
captures the first path, then supplies the second path and verifies the first
file remains effective.

